---
import GlassLayout from '../layouts/GlassLayout.astro';
---
<GlassLayout
  title="MBBS in Nepal Admission Process 2025 — MEC Nepal Step by Step | NepalMBBS.in"
  description="The official MEC Nepal admission process for Indian students, step by step: eligibility, NEET requirement, entrance exam, counseling and document verification."
  path="/admission-process"
>
<div class="tab-pane on" id="pane-process">
<div class="container">
  <div class="tc rev"><div class="eyebrow">Step by Step</div><div class="sec-title">From NEET to Nepal MBBS</div><div class="sec-sub">Complete official roadmap — every step verified from NMC India and MEC Nepal sources.</div></div>
  <ol class="doc-steps">
    <li class="doc-step"><h3 class="doc-step-title">NEET Score & Eligibility</h3><p class="doc-step-body">Per NMC India FMGL Regulations 2021, minimum 50th percentile NEET (General/OBC) or 40th percentile (SC/ST) required to practice in India after foreign MBBS. Verify current rules at NMC before applying.</p><p class="doc-step-body" style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><a href="https://nmc.org.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="card-link">NMC India ↗</a></p></li>
    <li class="doc-step"><h3 class="doc-step-title">College Selection via MEC Nepal</h3><p class="doc-step-body">All Nepal MBBS admissions are regulated by the Medical Education Commission (MEC Nepal). Select only MEC-approved colleges that are also NMC India recognised. Verify both lists before deciding.</p><p class="doc-step-body" style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><a href="https://mec.gov.np" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="card-link">MEC Nepal ↗</a></p></li>
    <li class="doc-step"><h3 class="doc-step-title">Documents & Application</h3><p class="doc-step-body">Required: 10th+12th marksheets (notarised), NEET scorecard, valid passport, medical fitness certificate, character certificate. Apply via MEC Nepal official portal only.</p><p class="doc-step-body" style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><a href="https://entrance.mec.gov.np" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="card-link">MECEE Portal ↗</a></p></li>
    <li class="doc-step"><h3 class="doc-step-title">Seat Confirmation & Fee Payment</h3><p class="doc-step-body">MEC Nepal runs transparent seat-matching. Pay fees ONLY directly to the college — never to agents. Verify official MEC fee ceiling at mec.gov.np before any payment.</p><p class="doc-step-body" style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><a href="https://mec.gov.np/en/feeStructure" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="card-link">Official Fee Structure ↗</a></p></li>
    <li class="doc-step"><h3 class="doc-step-title">Travel to Nepal — no visa required</h3><p class="doc-step-body">Indian citizens don't need a visa for Nepal under the India-Nepal bilateral open border agreement. Valid Indian passport or Aadhaar card is sufficient. Direct buses and flights available.</p><p class="doc-step-body" style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><a data-act="click" data-do='[["switchTab","lifestyle"]]' class="card-link" style="cursor:pointer">Life in Nepal ↗</a></p></li>
    <li class="doc-step"><h3 class="doc-step-title">MBBS → NExT / FMGE → India Practice</h3><p class="doc-step-body">5.5 years total. After graduation: clear NExT or FMGE (by NBE India) + complete 1 year supervised internship in India → receive licence to practice medicine in India.</p><p class="doc-step-body" style="margin-top:var(--s-2)"><a href="https://natboard.edu.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="card-link">NBE India ↗</a></p></li>
  </ol>
  <!-- COLLEGE COMPARISON -->
  <div style="margin-top:60px" class="rev">
    <div class="eyebrow">Quick Comparison</div>
    <div class="sec-title">Nepal MBBS vs India Private MBBS</div>
    <div class="sec-sub">Factual comparison to help informed decision-making. Individual factors may vary.</div>
    <div style="overflow-x:auto;margin-top:24px">
    <table class="compare-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Factor</th><th>Nepal MBBS</th><th>India Private MBBS</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><strong>NEET Requirement</strong></td><td>✅ Yes (50th percentile min)</td><td>✅ Yes (varies by college)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Medium of Instruction</strong></td><td>✅ English</td><td>✅ English</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Duration</strong></td><td>5.5 years (incl. internship)</td><td>5.5 years (incl. internship)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>NMC India Recognition</strong></td><td>✅ Select colleges (verify)</td><td>✅ All NMC approved</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Visa Required</strong></td><td>✅ No visa for Indians</td><td>N/A (same country)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Language Barrier</strong></td><td>✅ Hindi widely understood</td><td>✅ None</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>After Graduation</strong></td><td>NExT/FMGE + 1yr India intern</td><td>Direct India practice</td></tr>
        <tr><td><strong>Typical Cost</strong></td><td>Contact for official MEC fees</td><td>₹50L–1.5Cr+ (varies)</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:12px;font-style:italic">* Cost comparison not provided to avoid misleading figures. Contact us for current official MEC Nepal fee structure. Always verify all information at official government sources.</p>
  </div>
</div>
</div>
</GlassLayout>
